{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And every article of goats' hair.</b> As I explained. Now, a garment—because it touched a corpse—is unclean. The reason [for 'with you'] is [that] every garment [remains] with you until you purify yourselves. Or the word תתחחטאו [you shall purify yourselves] is going out [i.e., distributed], and likewise והתאויתם [you shall long] (Numbers 11:4), for the boundary is the action."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The lemma cites Numbers 31:20. The final clause כי הגבול הוא הפעול (literally 'for the boundary is the action') is opaque; rendered hyper-literally. The reading 'going out' for the word תתחטאו likely refers to the phrase's syntactic distribution applying to all garments mentioned, paralleling the similar phenomenon in והתאויתם."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:59.892663939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}